! Social tiddlers ~ the plane speaks in tiddlers

Three entities carry the social plane: a PRINCIPAL at `@identities`, a CIRCLE at `@circles`, a
SESSION at `@sessions`. Each one lands as a tiddler at its own lar: URI.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The invariants

# ''TIDDLER-FIRST.'' Every principal, circle, session, presence and world-clock record lives inside
`tiddlers`. Nothing typed sits outside it — anything that did would owe a self-describing meme in
`tiddlers` anyway, and a TW5 field filter reaches none of it.
# ''A reader REFUSES rather than invents.'' Each typed reader returns null when its identifying field
goes missing — a principal with no `did`, a circle or session with no `id`. A record that cannot name
itself gets no default name.
# ''Defaulting stays WITHIN the record, never across it.'' A reader falls back only to another field
of the same tiddler — `displayName` to the id it already holds, `createdAt` to TW5's own `created`,
`kind` to `device`, a session `state` to `active`. An absent optional field stays absent rather than
arriving as an empty string.
# ''The capability fields MIRROR Keyhive, and gate nothing here.'' `verifyingKey` carries the Ed25519
basis for delegation and actor-id derivation; `encryptedShareHint` carries the BeeKEM share hint that
survives a membership change; `capabilityPolicy` and `capabilityToken` carry policy and proof. These
shapes describe what a record HOLDS — the gate that reads them stands in the keyhive package.
# ''Key history never decreases.'' `keyHistory` holds an append-only audit of `{ key, rotatedAt }`
pairs, so a rotation adds and a reader can walk back.
# ''A circle carries its own anti-replay.'' `nonceBurnSet` holds the burned nonces for inbound
invites, and `memberSignature` signs the member set together with the circle's id, name and scope — so
a membership claim travels with the thing that proves it.
# ''Presence stays ephemeral and clock-bearing.'' A `PresenceSlot` carries cursor, viewport, selection
and a map of FFZ clocks. It names live attention rather than durable membership.

<<~/ahu>>

